# Spring Boot template (agents)

Java 21 · Spring Boot 4.1 · package-by-feature monolith. Human runbook: `README.md`. Agent pack: `.agents/`.

## Layout

```text
src/main/java/.../springboottemplate/
  app/        # shared: config, BaseEntity, exceptions, utils, debug controllers
  auth/       # JWT, OAuth2, SecurityConfig, roles, token blacklist
  user/       # UserEntity, profile, verification/status
  article/    # sample CRUD + @Cacheable detail
  email/      # MailService + Thymeleaf handlers
src/main/resources/
  application.yml           # base + spring.profiles.default=dev
  application-dev.yml       # local debug
  application-prod.yml      # deploy
  db/migration/             # Flyway only
src/test/...                # mirror packages; profile test (H2, no Redis)
```

## How to work

1. Read neighboring code in the same feature package before changing patterns.
2. Prefer the smallest diff that solves the task; no drive-by refactors.
3. New domain capability → new/extended **feature package**, not dumping into `app`.
4. After Java edits: `./mvnw spotless:apply`, then run the smallest relevant tests.
5. Local API needs Postgres + Redis: `docker compose up -d app-postgres-db app-redis`.
6. Adding a domain feature (`order`, …): use skill **add-feature** (`.agents/skills/add-feature`) and clone the `article` package.
7. Refactor / dọn code / align conventions: use skill **refactor-code** (`.agents/skills/refactor-code`). Smallest diff; do not rewrite auth/Redis.

## Commands

```bash
./mvnw spotless:apply
./mvnw test                     # local iterate
./mvnw -Dtest=ClassNameTest test
./mvnw verify                   # CI / pre-merge (test + package)
./mvnw spring-boot:run          # profile dev by default
./mvnw -DskipTests package
```

## Profiles

| Profile | Role |
|---------|------|
| `dev` | Default local (`spring.profiles.default=dev`) |
| `prod` | Deploy; Compose `app-api` default |
| `test` | Maven tests only |

Do not put `spring.profiles.default` inside `application-*.yml` profile files.

## Never without an explicit ask

- Commit `.env` / real secrets
- Add Redisson or a second Redis client
- Move token blacklist onto Spring `CacheManager`
- Replace JWT with server sessions
- Re-enable Redis (or mail) health so probes fail when Redis is down
- Broad refactors, new frameworks, or rewriting working auth
